# Project conventions

- **Done means green:** `{{packageManager}} run check`, `{{packageManager}} run test` and `{{packageManager}} run build` pass. `check` runs the type-check, ESLint (strict type-checked rules, naming, complexity and module boundaries), Prettier and Knip.
- **Structure:** routes in `src/app/` stay thin and delegate to `src/features/<domain>/`; a feature imports only itself, `src/lib/`, `src/components/` and the project infrastructure. `src/lib/` knows no feature.
- **Tests:** Vitest, next to the file under test (`*.test.ts`); server modules import as on the server.{{#if api}} Procedures are called in-process (see `src/features/health/server/router.test.ts`).{{/if}}{{#if (usesTestDatabase)}} `@/lib/database` is an in-process PGlite database per test file, migrated from `./drizzle` — run `{{packageManager}} run db:generate` after a schema change.{{/if}}{{#if (and (usesTestDatabase) (eq auth "better-auth"))}} `createSignedInUser()` (`src/test/`) returns a session's headers{{#if (eq api.type "trpc")}}; resolve them with `auth.api.getSession({ headers })` for a tRPC caller's `session`{{/if}}.{{/if}}
- **Environment:** `src/env.ts` is the only module that reads `process.env`. A new variable goes into `src/env.ts` and `.env.example` together.
{{#if (or api (eq auth "better-auth") (and production database))}}
- **Logging:** server code logs through `@/lib/logger` (pino), object first, message second, the error under `err`. Never `console`.
{{/if}}
{{#if (or api (eq auth "better-auth"))}}
- **Client IP:** {{#if (eq auth "better-auth")}}Better-Auth's rate limits and {{/if}}the security logs read the client IP from `x-real-ip`, which only a proxy that overwrites it makes trustworthy — the generated nginx does. Behind another proxy, switch `CLIENT_IP_HEADER` in `src/lib/client-ip.ts` to the header that proxy sets.
{{/if}}
{{#if (or api (eq auth "better-auth"))}}
- **Errors:** an expected failure is an `AppError`. Common codes come from `commonErrors` (`@/lib/errors/common-errors`); a feature declares codes only for rules it enforces itself, in its own `errors.ts` with `defineErrors({ CODE: { status, message } })`, and never renames another layer's code.{{#if api}} `publicProcedure` maps errors to the API once; procedures start from `{{#if (eq auth "better-auth")}}protectedProcedure{{else}}publicProcedure{{/if}}`.{{/if}}{{#if (eq auth "better-auth")}} Server calls to `auth.api` that can fail go through `callAuth` (`getSession` answers `null` instead).{{/if}}
- **Error messages:** the client turns any error into text with `toErrorMessage(error, overrides?)` (`@/lib/errors/display/error-messages`); a feature passes overrides only where the default text does not fit.{{#if (eq auth "better-auth")}} Client calls to `authClient` go through `runAuthRequest` (`@/lib/auth/errors/auth-request`), which returns the message or nothing.{{/if}}{{#if api}} Mutations toast their errors centrally — set `meta: { showsErrorInForm: true }` when a form shows the error itself, `meta.errorMessages` for feature texts.{{/if}}
{{/if}}
{{#if api.openapi}}
- **Public API:** `/api/v1` and its spec serve only `publicApiRouter` (`src/orpc/routers/public-api-router.ts`), never the whole `appRouter`. A procedure joins it deliberately and one by one, with a `.route()`; never nest a whole feature router there, since oRPC would serve each of its procedures, even those without `.route()`, as `POST /api/v1/<path>`.
{{/if}}

